# What the source distribution carries beyond the package itself.
#
# Without this file setuptools applies its own defaults, and those defaults ship `tests/test*.py`
# but not `tests/shipped.py` — a helper every prohibition gate imports. Measured 2026-09-21 on a
# built artefact: nine test files arrived, their shared import did not, and `pytest` stopped at
# "Interrupted: 2 errors during collection". Zero of 123 tests ran, while the README promised
# that every behavioural claim could be checked by running them.
#
# The rule this encodes: the README's verification table names files, so those files ship.
# The repo-only files ship too, so that the gates below walk the SAME surface in both
# channels. Teaching them to expect two different trees would put the control arm on a
# different path from the thing it controls — and the sdist is then no longer the repo.
include .gitignore
recursive-include .github *.yml

include CITATION.cff
include NOTICE
include MANIFEST.in
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include examples *.py
